Benchmark data and evaluation code
----------------------------------
The Benchmarks section vendors three datasets and ports part of one
evaluator. Each is used under its own license, as follows.

- EvalPlus (https://github.com/evalplus/evalplus), Apache License 2.0; the
  full text is LICENSE_EVALPLUS in this directory.
  - The datasets HumanEval+ v0.1.10 and MBPP+ v0.2.0, the release assets of
    evalplus/humanevalplus_release and evalplus/mbppplus_release,
    unmodified, in apps/server/local_llm/benchmarks/data/datasets/
    humanevalplus/ and mbppplus/.
  - Functions ported from EvalPlus v0.3.1 into
    apps/server/local_llm/benchmarks/evaluation/grading/evalplus_runtime.py:
    - the special oracles, from evalplus/eval/_special_oracle.py;
    - the MBPP+ input deserializer, from evalplus/data/mbpp.py;
    - the output comparison (is_floats and the loop body of
      unsafe_execute), from evalplus/eval/__init__.py, rewritten to run
      without numpy;
    - the time-limit defaults, from evalplus/config.py;
    - the expected-output computation, from evalplus/gen/util/__init__.py;
    - the answer sanitizer (sanitize, extract_target_code_or_empty,
      code_extract), from evalplus/sanitize.py, rewritten on Python's ast
      instead of tree-sitter.
  - The chat instruction in the humanevalplus and mbppplus adapters, from
    evalplus/codegen.py and evalplus/provider/openai.py.

